---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About - Gabriele Radicello">
  <section
    class="mx-auto flex min-h-[70vh] flex-col items-center justify-center gap-10 md:gap-16 px-6 pt-28 md:pt-64 pb-16 md:pb-20 text-left"
  >
    <div class="max-w-5xl">
      <div
        class="columns-1 md:columns-2 gap-12 text-lg leading-7 md:leading-8 text-neutral-300 text-left md:text-justify hyphens-none"
        lang="en"
      >
        <p class="mb-6 md:mb-8 break-inside-avoid">
          Gabriele Radicello is a multimedia artist whose practice delves into
          the intricate web of relationships between human sensitivity and
          algorithmic computation. Driven by a continuous push for innovation,
          his work is founded on the concept of symbiosis: a complex state where
          human beings and the digital ecosystem do not exist in isolation, but
          constantly influence and redefine each other through an uninterrupted
          dialogue.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6 md:mb-8 break-inside-avoid">
          Shaped by a deep investigation into network cultures and the
          exploration of virtual worlds, the artist acts as an observer of the
          new landscapes generated by code. His practice merges a critical
          awareness of the technological medium with the creation of synthetic
          architectures that serve as true extensions of the psyche.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6 md:mb-8 break-inside-avoid">
          Gabriele Radicello explores the liminal and uncanny spaces that reside
          on the boundary between the organic and the computational, advocating
          for the dissolution of the self-imposed distance between biology and
          machine in search of a post-organic aesthetic that makes the richness
          of this convergence tangible.
        </p>
        <p class="break-inside-avoid">
          Through his work, the artist questions the very nature of the creative
          process and the algorithmic sublime, structurally integrating
          artificial intelligence into his research. Embracing the
          unpredictability of latent spaces and data, AI is never employed as a
          mere executive tool, but elevated to the role of co-creator. Through
          works with a strong immersive resonance, Gabriele Radicello invites
          the viewer to reconsider the boundaries between the human and the
          synthetic, encouraging a deeper understanding of the complex hybrid
          choreography that defines our present.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="grid gap-12 border-t border-neutral-700 pt-12 md:grid-cols-2 w-full max-w-4xl text-left"
    >
      <section>
        <h2
          class="mb-4 text-3xl font-normal text-neutral-50"
          style="font-family: 'Helvetica Custom', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;"
        >
          Exhibitions
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-inside list-disc text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-400">
          <li>
            2026 <a href="https://www.cityopenmuseum.com/la-fura-dels-baus/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white transition-colors">Codice Umano</a> (La Fura dels Baus x Accademia di Belle Arti di Carrara). ex Ceramica Vaccari, Santo Stefano Magra
          </li>
          <li>
            2026 <a href="https://www.cityopenmuseum.com/last-gesture-premiazione/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white transition-colors">Last Gesture Festival</a> — Winner of Audience Award for "The Innovation Dilemma". Accademia di Belle Arti di Carrara
          </li>
          <li>
            2025-26 <a href="https://accademiacarrara.it/extra-bold-festival-di-sperimentazione-visiva/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white transition-colors">EXTRABOLD Festival</a> Live Media. City Open Museum Carrara
          </li>
          <li>2025 Annual Exhibition. Academy of Fine Arts Carrara</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2
          class="mb-4 text-3xl font-normal text-neutral-50"
          style="font-family: 'Helvetica Custom', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;"
        >
          Education
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-inside list-disc text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-400">
          <li>Multimedia Arts High School, Viareggio</li>
          <li>Academy of Fine Arts, Carrara</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

  </section>
</BaseLayout>
